    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe acceptance test requires the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response to include a `timezone` field derived from the owner's region via the fixed table `NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`.\n\nThe owner response is assembled by `OwnerMapper`, where every derived field (e.g. `locality`) delegates to a small util. I followed that exact idiom:\n\n1. **`util/Timezone.java`** (new, small cohesive unit) \u2014 a single `of(region)` method backed by the fixed region\u2192timezone map. WMC_other \u2248 0, CC = 1.\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line for `timezone`, reusing the existing `CustomerCode.region(...)` derivation already used for `locality`. No existing method grew in complexity.\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nStructural impact is kept low: the only pre-existing function edited is the mapper's `toOwnerDto` (a single new annotation line), and the new behaviour lives in a fresh, near-zero-complexity class rather than growing any existing class.\n\nUnknown regions map to `null` (field omitted), consistent with the existing `\"UNKNOWN\"` locality handling.",
